# Copy to agent-memory-backup.env beside the installed scripts (for example
# ~/agent-memory-backup/bin/) and set this machine's values. The copy is never
# committed; the repo's .gitignore is an allowlist.
#
# Read by backup_agent_memory_pg.sh, backup_runner.py and
# restore_test_agent_memory.sh. AGENT_MEMORY_BACKUP_ENV=/path/to/file names
# another file. A variable that is already set in the environment (a cron line,
# a test, an override on the command line) wins over this file.
#
# Format: KEY=VALUE, one per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are
# skipped. An optional "export " and one pair of surrounding quotes are
# removed. Nothing is expanded or executed: no $VAR, no $(...), no ~, and no
# comment after a value. No secret belongs here; the dump runs as the
# container's own POSTGRES_USER through docker exec.
#
# Keep the nightly configuration here, never on the cron line, so cron,
# status, list, verify, dry-run and an on-demand run all read the same paths.

# The NAS share's mount point and the published backup inside it.
MOUNTPOINT=/mnt/nas
DEST_ROOT=/mnt/nas/backups/agent-memory-postgres

# A local drive with room for one dump plus LOCAL_MIN_FREE_KB (60 GiB), not
# the disk that holds the live Postgres.
LOCAL_STAGING=/srv/backup-staging/agent-memory-backup/staging

# The "OK|BUSY <utc>" line a probe on the NAS side writes onto the share. The
# copy writes only while it says OK and is fresh. PACE_GATE=0 turns the gate
# off.
POOL_STATE_FILE=/mnt/nas/.nas-tuning/pool_state
# PACE_GATE=1

# install-cron puts this in front of the runner when its first word is an
# executable, for example a wrapper that runs the job in a MemoryHigh scope.
# Empty installs the plain line.
# CACHE_WRAP="/usr/local/bin/run-in-memory-scope --high 4G --"
CACHE_WRAP=

# Copy pacing. BWLIMIT_KBPS on the cron line (install-cron writes it there)
# wins over a value here.
# BWLIMIT_KBPS=6000
# TRANSFER_WINDOW_UTC=07:00-13:00
# CRON_SCHEDULE="20 2 * * *"

# restore_test_agent_memory.sh: the drive that holds LOCAL_STAGING (the test
# image goes there), and an optional systemd unit whose speed it watches.
STAGING_DRIVE=/srv/backup-staging
# SERVING_UNIT=my-inference-server
